 # In-Brick DDA for Occlusion
 ## Overview
-A Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) that marches through a 4×4×4 voxel brick to determine if any solid voxel occludes a shadow ray [S1, unofficial]. Unlike primary hit resolution which stops at the first intersection, this method visits all solid voxels within the brick to correctly handle transparent or fringe cases [S1, unofficial].
+A Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) that marches through a 4×4×4 voxel brick to determine if any solid voxel occludes a shadow ray [S1, unofficial]. Unlike primary hit resolution which stops at the first intersection, this method visits all solid voxels within the brick to correctly handle transparent or fringe cases [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Hardware Ray Tracing Voxel Occlusion](3631-hardware-ray-tracing-voxel-occlusion.md) and [RDV-1 Occupancy Ray Query](12302-rdv-1-occupancy-ray-query.md) by explicitly iterating a fixed number of steps within a single brick rather than relying on hardware acceleration or hierarchical occupancy queries.
 
